WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.089
Film Courage: FYI (Films By Youth Inside) that is your
nonprofit? Alex Munoz, Founder of FYI Films/Filmmaker: Yes. Film Courage: Do you remember the day

00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:11.309
that you not just applied for the
the nonprofit status but that you

00:00:11.309 --> 00:00:17.220
actually came up with the idea to do it?
Alex: Yes, I wish I could say I had this

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:22.460
great idea to teach filmmaking to
incarcerated youth but it actually was a

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:29.609
result of as a consequence of my my
encounter with a group of community

00:00:29.609 --> 00:00:34.290
activists when I did my first movie
about the LA riots [1992] for a short time

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:38.219
which investigated the civil unrest
following the Rodney King verdict. We

00:00:38.219 --> 00:00:43.200
screened the film at first AME Church
and leaders from the Latino community,

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:48.899
Korean American community, African
American community and also LAPD [Los Angeles Police Department] people

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:54.000
were there to have a panel discussion
and the screening was shut down by a

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:01.530
group of about 20 to 22 young black
activists who said "F' Hollywood! You guys

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:05.670
don't offer any jobs training or
workforce development. We have all these

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:09.750
young brothers and sisters who want to
get in. You just come in here and make

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:15.330
your films and don't talk to us. What
needs to happen for our people from our

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:20.009
community to enter your industry?" And
they set the screening down for two

00:01:20.009 --> 00:01:25.409
hours and a lot of producers left. They
said "You are discriminating against

00:01:25.409 --> 00:01:30.990
people of color and people from
disadvantaged communities this is nonsense. We

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:38.100
want answers now!" So it was good that the
producers heard this it was important

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:43.020
and finally Reverend Cecil Mary said
"Let's show the film and let's talk

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:48.270
more after." And I went up to these young
activists and I said "Hey, I don't

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:54.570
think it's fair to depict all Hollywood
filmmakers as uncaring. I'm interested in

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:58.350
doing what I can." They said "We'll prove
it!" And I said "Well how do you want me to

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:02.460
prove it?" And they said "Go to Herman G. Stark [Youth Correction Facility in Chino, CA] where they consummate the most

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:07.649
violent youth offenders and tell them
about your journey. Tell them about what

00:02:07.649 --> 00:02:10.800
you do, that you went to USC [University Southern California], that you're
a professional filmmaker. Be a role model

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:17.410
to them." So two weeks later I go
Herman G. Stark and I'm given a uniseg

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:22.720
which is this round device it looks like
a pager and they said if you feel in

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.110
danger pulled a pin and within 10
seconds the SWAT team will enter your

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:30.940
room and I'm thinking oh my god what did
I get myself into so I'm in this room

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:35.590
full of 35 young men while see Latino
and black males covered with tattoos, ankles

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:47.350
cuffed, a lot of sadness in their eyes, a
lot of depression and dimness you

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:53.350
know? And I start talking to them and
about an hour and a half into my

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:57.760
presentation I leave the room to use the
restroom and I had sip my favorite pair

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:03.280
of Maui Jim sunglasses on the chalkboard
and like $250 and my favorite pair of

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:08.230
sunglasses so I came back into the room
and they were gone and so I just figured

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:11.410
I'll talk about this before I leave so
at the end of the three hour

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:16.930
presentation I said hey guys I came in
here with my favorite pair of sunglasses

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:20.380
and I drove all the way out here it took
like an hour and 20 minutes like I like

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:23.890
them back but I won't tell anybody would
happen no one's gonna get in trouble so

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:27.400
I'm gonna leave the room you guys talk
amongst yourselves and I'll come back

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:32.350
two minutes and let's try to find the
resolution so I left the room when it's

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:38.049
a hallway got a glass of water just had
quiet time and then I came back and I

00:03:38.049 --> 00:03:42.609
said okay so can someone tell me where
my sunglasses are and a black and Latino

00:03:42.609 --> 00:03:48.370
